  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>}</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>}</mo></math>. Total number of onto functions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>S</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, is equal to ________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "180",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>}</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>}</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0075_887da195131a.png\" style=\"width: 227px; height: 171px;\" /></p><p>Now taking,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;one of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;then total such cases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math><br />Now if,&nbsp;only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then we have distribute&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;amongst&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,<br />So, total cases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math><br />So, number&nbsp;of onto functions when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math></p><p>Now finding, total number&nbsp;of onto functions,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>973</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>192</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn></math><br />Number of required functions when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
